---
import CaseContents from "./CaseContents.astro";
---
<article class="malibu-case">
  <header class="intro"><div class="meta case-meta"><span class="case-meta__client-full">Malibu Rum / Pernod Ricard USA</span><span class="case-meta__client-short">Malibu Rum</span><span class="case-meta__highlight">60M impressions</span><span class="case-meta__role">Senior UX Strategist &amp; Creative Lead</span></div><div class="intro__grid"><div><p class="index">Creative Systems &amp; Campaign Design</p><h1>101 Days<br />of <span class="heading-accent">Because</span><br />Summer</h1></div><p class="lede">Malibu's 101 Days of Because Summer required daily content across Facebook, Instagram, and its website, from recipe graphics to live activations and animation.</p></div></header>
  <CaseContents links={[{"href": "#case-section-1", "label": "Strategy"}, {"href": "#case-section-2", "label": "Creative system"}, {"href": "#case-section-3", "label": "Campaign"}, {"href": "#case-section-4", "label": "Results"}]} />
  <figure class="hero"><img src="/images/malibu-rum_hero.webp" alt="Friends toasting colorful summer drinks under a blue sky" loading="eager" decoding="async" /></figure>
<section class="malibu-detail" aria-labelledby="malibu-brief"><div><p class="malibu-detail__label">The brief</p><h2 id="malibu-brief">One campaign, produced by several teams.</h2></div><div class="malibu-detail__copy"><p>As Senior UX Strategist and Creative Lead through Pocket Made, I defined the visual system, built the toolkit, and reviewed production so participating teams could work from shared decisions.</p></div></section>
  <section class="audit" id="case-section-1" tabindex="-1"><div><p class="index">01 / The foundation</p><h2>Research &amp; Brand<br />Consistency Analysis</h2></div><div class="copy"><p>An audit of two previous summer seasons identified inconsistent color, typography, and asset production; stronger-performing content featuring real ingredients, everyday settings, and informal moments informed the direction.</p><p>Testing existing guidelines against planned formats exposed missing rules for dark backgrounds, motion, and co-branding.</p></div><div class="audit__art"><img src="/images/malibu01.webp" alt="Campaign overview and engagement model" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><img src="/images/malibu02.webp" alt="Malibu social campaign examples" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div></section>
  <section class="sensation" id="case-section-2" tabindex="-1"><div><p class="index">02 / The visual system</p><h2>Summer as<br /><span class="heading-accent">Sensation</span></h2><div class="copy"><p>Aqua teals, sun-bleached oranges, woodgrain, lime peel, and grill textures expressed summer through physical detail.</p><p>Hand-painted headlines, rounded sans-serif copy, layered photography, and vector overlays carried that informal character across formats.</p></div></div><figure><img src="/images/malibu03.webp" alt="101 Days of Because Summer campaign visual language" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure><figure><img src="/images/malibu04.webp" alt="Malibu-Q activation creative" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>
  <section class="toolkit" id="case-section-3" tabindex="-1"><div class="toolkit__title"><p class="index">03 / Production at scale</p><h2>200+ Assets Built<br />for Production Speed</h2></div><div class="toolkit__images"><figure><img src="/images/malibu05.webp" alt="Malibu product creative assets" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure><figure><img src="/images/malibu06.webp" alt="Malibu summer lifestyle photography" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></div><div class="copy"><p>More than 200 logos, stickers, icons, type treatments, layouts, and composited backgrounds provided editable Photoshop and vector material. Templates covered 16:9, 1:1, and 9:16, including static and carousel grids, to support adaptation.</p><p>A thirty-minute onboarding target shaped file organization, labels, and documentation; it was a design standard, not a measured usability result.</p></div></section>
<section class="malibu-detail" aria-labelledby="malibu-review"><div><p class="malibu-detail__label">Execution &amp; ownership</p><h2 id="malibu-review">Keep the system useful during production.</h2></div><div class="malibu-detail__copy"><p>I reviewed motion from storyboards through final cuts and coordinated release scheduling with content strategists, while Pocket Made's animation and content teams shared asset production.</p></div></section>
  <section class="results" id="case-section-4" tabindex="-1"><div><p class="index">04 / Results</p><h2>Results &amp;<br />Multi-Market Adoption</h2></div><div class="numbers"><div><b>25%</b><span>increase in social engagement</span></div><div><b>60M</b><span>combined impressions</span></div><div><b>101</b><span>consecutive days on-brand</span></div></div><div class="copy"><p>The original project account reports 25% higher social engagement than the prior summer and 60 million combined paid and organic impressions. These are campaign-level figures, not isolated effects of the design system.</p><p>It also records adoption in four international markets, 101 publishing days without a missed date, and no brand-consistency escalations. Shared assets and rules supported that distributed production.</p></div></section>
<section class="malibu-detail" aria-labelledby="malibu-reflection"><div><p class="malibu-detail__label">Reflection</p><h2 id="malibu-reflection">Bring every production team in earlier.</h2></div><div class="malibu-detail__copy"><p>Some interpretation gaps still appeared during production, so I would review a common sample brief with every agency before finalizing the toolkit.</p><p>Testing dark backgrounds, co-branding, motion, and aspect-ratio changes together would expose differences before launch.</p></div></section>
</article>
<style>
